"{\"edits\":[{\"start\":0,\"end\":1,\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"For January 15, the Vancouver Aeroplan economy award may suit you if a 6:30 a.m. arrival in Bangkok on January 17 and nine reported seats matter. It requires 92,144 points and has a CAD 43.90 taxes-and-fees quote (scope unknown). It arrives later than the noon Taiwan option, which requires fewer points, but its reported seat count is higher; the record does not establish the cabin on each flight. The search results are partial, availability may change, and the award fee quotes have unknown scope.\"},{\"k\":\"p\",\"r\":\"J20@2027-01-15T17:15-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T06:30\",\"n\":\"Vancouver award — 6:30 a.m. arrival\",\"v\":\"Aeroplan economy award from SFO via YVR to BKK, departing January 15 at 5:15 p.m. and arriving January 17 at 6:30 a.m. The record reports 92,144 Aeroplan points, CAD 43.90 in taxes and fees (quote scope unknown), and nine seats. One stop; the connection at YVR is 217 minutes. Consider it if the earlier arrival and higher reported seat count appeal; compared with the noon Taiwan option it requires more points and arrives 5 hours 5 minutes later. The record does not specify the cabin of either leg.\"}]},{\"start\":3,\"end\":6,\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J7@2027-01-15T12:00-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T01:25\",\"n\":\"Earlier Taiwan arrival\",\"v\":\"Aeroplan economy award via TPE on BR, departing January 15 at noon and arriving January 17 at 1:25 a.m. Requires 65,000 Aeroplan points, plus a CAD 116.50 fee quote of unknown scope; one seat is reported. The TPE connection is 270 minutes. Compared with the Vancouver option, it requires fewer points and arrives 5 hours 5 minutes earlier, but has one reported seat rather than nine, a higher fee quote, and a connection 53 minutes longer. It also departs 5 hours 15 minutes earlier; the leg-by-leg cabins are not stated.\"},{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J15@2027-01-15T23:30-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T11:10\",\"n\":\"Late-night Taiwan departure\",\"v\":\"Aeroplan economy award via TPE on BR, departing January 15 at 11:30 p.m. and arriving January 17 at 11:10 a.m. Requires 65,000 Aeroplan points, plus a CAD 116.50 fee quote of unknown scope; one seat is reported. The TPE connection is 145 minutes. Compared with the Vancouver option, it requires fewer points, has a lower fee quote, and a shorter connection, but arrives 4 hours 40 minutes later and reports one seat rather than nine. Leg-by-leg cabins are not stated.\"},{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J13@2027-01-15T23:30-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T16:50\",\"n\":\"Later Taiwan arrival\",\"v\":\"Aeroplan economy award via TPE on BR and TG, departing January 15 at 11:30 p.m. and arriving January 17 at 4:50 p.m. Requires 65,000 Aeroplan points, plus a CAD 116.50 fee quote of unknown scope; one seat is reported. The TPE connection is 495 minutes. Compared with the Vancouver option, it requires fewer points and has a lower fee quote, but arrives 10 hours 20 minutes later, has one reported seat rather than nine, and has a connection 278 minutes longer. The record does not state the cabin on each leg.\"}]},{\"start\":6,\"end\":7,\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"If you prefer a cash fare rather than using award points, the search also returned this one-stop itinerary. Its quoted price scope is unknown, so do not assume it is a per-person or all-in total.\"}]},{\"start\":8,\"end\":9,\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"Shared cautions: these are selected examples, not the full inventory; the source reports a partial search and some results may not be real-time. Confirm current availability and pricing with the booking provider. Award-fee quote scope is unknown, points and cash are separate, and no complete award cost can be established from these quotes. An award economy label does not confirm every leg’s cabin. The cash and award routes include connections; the records do not establish ticket protection or other booking conditions.\"}]}]}"
